# CERT CATALOG UI SLICE 1 — diff for gate review (theme only, NOT promoted). Build order: claude/B4C_CertCatalog_UI_Slice1_BuildOrder.md
# Test: HAPPY_DOM_DIR=<dir with happy-dom> node docs/review/cert_catalog_ui_slice1_test.mjs  ->  33 passed, 0 failed (output at the end).
# Regression: expirations 8/0 · scorecard 23/0 · onboarding config 22/0 · event details 34/0 · eslint . clean · vite build ok.
# Files: src/App.jsx + shared/expiry.js only. No DB migration. update_cert / delete_cert calls byte-identical. Locked-token count unchanged.
#
# HOW neverExpires IS THREADED THROUGH THE certStatus CALL SITES
#   Source of the flag: each cert row now carries certTypeId (both cert selects add cert_type_id); enrichCerts(certs, typeMap)
#   adds neverExpires / typeName / typeCategory from the dept_cert_types() catalog (loaded in the SAME Promise.all as the
#   roster; a failed catalog read keeps the last-known catalog). A catalog change re-enriches members in place (one
#   useEffect on the map), and an assign patches + re-enriches the one row — so every cert object in `members` (and the
#   self-merge row) already has c.neverExpires by the time any badge renders. Untyped / deleted-type certs enrich to false.
#   Signature: certStatus(exp, neverExpires = false) — the new branch is the FIRST line: neverExpires -> NO EXPIRY, rank 2.
#   All 13 call sites hold the cert object, so each passes c.neverExpires (mechanical, nothing else on the line moved):
#     PersonalView open-loops (rank <= 1)          · PersonalView all certs (me.certs)       · dashboard flagged (rank < 2)
#     certCoverage (r === 1 || r === 2, undated r=3) · RosterMembers compliance (rank === 2) · MemberDetail cert list
#     RosterCerts rows (also carries neverExpires for its phrase) · RosterCerts compliantN (1||2, !0) · byCert exp/old
#     report ranks (cm certs) · Chief's report flaggedCerts (rank < 2) · business-meeting certRows · DA-dashboard expdC (=== 0)
#   Because NO EXPIRY is rank 2 (= CURRENT), every one of those predicates gives the same answer it gives a current cert —
#   no comparison, filter or count was edited; only the label ("NO EXPIRY") / colour (CURRENT's #2E7D52) differ.
#   expPhrase(exp, neverExpires) got the same optional arg ("Doesn't expire") at the 6 places that show a typed cert's line;
#   the 3 left bare are rank-1/flagged-only lists (a never-expires cert can't appear there) and the pending-submission queue
#   (submissions have no type yet).
#   The test proves it: certCoverage + the compliance predicate return identical results for {exp:null, neverExpires:true}
#   and a current cert; an untyped blank cert still counts undated.
#
# DEVIATIONS / NOTES
#   - The mock's "renews every N yrs" line has no backing column (cert_types has no interval) — the list shows the
#     linked-cert count + Expires / Doesn't expire instead.
#   - Cert Types lives on Roster -> Certifications as a collapsible "Cert types · Manage" card, gated isDeptAdmin (DA / PA);
#     Delete additionally needs useCanDeleteShared (the typed-phrase gate, DA / PA — same set).
#   - The assign picker is gated isDeptAdmin(role) (mirrors assign_cert_type), placed beside View proof / Edit / Remove.
#   - rdItemDetail's "This qualification is inactive" (readiness-requirement path) is untouched — Slice 2.

